alar recurrence for entire horizontal scan with unrolling by 4 using independent accumulators initialized at positions 0..3 and process blocks while `j + 8 <= limit`, then finish tail from j+4 using a single accumulator derived from w[3]. This is manageable.\n\nLet's implement helper:\n\n```\nstatic inline long long maxWindow(const long long* c, int n, int s) {\n    int limit = n - s;\n    if (limit < 0) return LLONG_MIN; // not happen\n    long long w0=0,w1=0,w2=0,w3=0;\n    for(int j=0;j<s;++j) w0 += c[j];\n    long long best = w0;\n    int cnt = limit + 1;\n    if(cnt > 1){ w1 = w0 - c[0] + c[s]; if(w1>best) best=w1; }\n    if(cnt > 2){ w2 = w1 - c[1] + c[s+1]; if(w2>best) best=w2; }\n    if(cnt > 3){ w3 = w2 - c[2] + c[s+2]; if(w3>best) best=w3; }\n\n    int j=0;\n    while (j + 8 <= limit) {\n        // current windows at j..j+3\n        w0 += c[j+s] - c[j];\n        w1 += c[j+1+s] - c[j+1];\n        w2 += c[j+2+s] - c[j+2];\n        w3 += c[j+3+s] - c[j+3];\n        if(w0>best) best=w0;\n        ...\n        j += 4;\n    }\n    // Now current windows at positions j..j+3 (all <= limit? because loop condition ensured previous update targets valid; after final iteration, new j = old+4 and max index old+7 <= limit due condition, so yes all four <=limit)\n    int last = j + 3;\n    if(last > limit) { // shouldn't happen?\n        last = limit;\n    }\n    long long cur = (last >= j ? (last==j?w0: last==j+1?w1: ... ) : w0);\n```\nBut after loop, we have already compared current windows when they were computed. We need compute from `last+1` to limit.\nIf limit <= j+3, no tail needed because all remaining positions up to limit are among current and already compared (but if some current >limit invalid not used). If limit > j+3, then tail exists.\n\nLet's set:\n```\nint pos = j + 4;\nif(pos <= limit) {\n   long long cur = w3; // W[j+3]\n   for(int p=pos; p<=limit; ++p) {\n      cur += c[p+s-1] - c[p-1]; // since W[p]=W[p-1]+c[p-1+s]-c[p-1], with previous index p-1\n    